# Line endings are not a style preference here, they decide whether afox runs.
#
# roles.mjs parses roles.yml and providers.yml line by line, and its top-level
# scalar regex ends in (.*)$ — (.*) cannot match a carriage return and $ does not
# match before one, so with CRLF every key fails to match and falls through the
# ignore branch. The symptom is `roles.yml: missing "repo"` against a file where
# repo: . is plainly present. A CR at the end of a shebang is likewise a bad
# interpreter naming a shell that is installed.
#
# The repository's blobs have always been LF; it is Windows checkout under
# core.autocrlf=true that introduces the CR. Pinning eol=lf changes no blob, so
# it is invisible on macOS and Linux and is the whole fix on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf
